Design for Automated Disassembly is a key part of the Design for Disassembly strategy. Although most products can be disassembled by human labour, this may lead to high operational costs and time consumption. Developing automatic and systemic disassembly may overcome this obstacle and improve the economic feasibility of disassembly.  This strategy involves the use of robots equipped with artificial intelligence (AI) that are able to scan the physical condition of the product and disassembling it, even if the product is highly worn. Robots are also flexible and able to recognize the product typology and adapt their operations accordingly with it. This process requires a high level of mechanical and control system to be achieved,